SUMMARY:Deadline: SUPPORT 2028 Festival Open Call for Artworks (Smartwear R
 evolution\, University of Alberta)
DESCRIPTION:Open call for new or existing artworks\, performances and fashi
 on collections on support\, disability\, smart textiles\, technology\, acc
 ess and embodiment for the SUPPORT 2028 festival at University of Alberta 
 venues including FAB Gallery\, the Sound Studies Institute gallery and the
  Timms Centre. About five visual artists\, three fashion designers and two
  performance groups will be selected.\n\nOrganisation: Co-Designing a Smar
 twear Revolution\, University of Alberta (Art & Design Working Group)\, fu
 nded by the New Frontiers in Research Fund\nLocation: Edmonton\, Alberta\,
  Canada (University of Alberta venues\, May 2028\; every work must exist i
 n person and online). Open to national and international artists.\nAward: 
 Artist fees at CARFAC/CADA recommended rates (e.g. CAD 1\,094 for a group 
 show of more than five artists)\, installation and shipping covered\, prod
 uction fees possible\, and a CAD 50 to 100 honorarium for stage-2 proposal
 s. No application fee.\nDuration: Festival in May 2028\n\nMore: https://sm
 artwearrevolution.com/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://smartwearrevolution.com/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Edmonton\, Alberta\, Canada (University of Alberta venues\, May 20
 28\; every work must exist in person and online). Open to national and int
 ernational artists.
END:VEVENT
